<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodoric II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 466</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-ii-king-of-the-visigoths">Theodoric II</a> was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 453 to 466, having taken power by killing his brother Thorismund. An ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, he backed the elevation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avitus">Avitus</a> as emperor in 455 and in 456 destroyed the Suebic army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astorga">Astorga</a>, later executing its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rechiar">Rechiar</a>. He was murdered by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euric">Euric</a>, who succeeded him.</p></div>
